Subject: [R-pkg-team] Bug#1010997: ITP: r-cran-leidenbase -- GNU R and C/C++
 Wrappers to Run the Leiden find_partition() Function
Message-ID: <165256475352.491348.10039392077194333129.reportbug@sputnik.fam-tille.de>

Package: wnpp
Severity: wishlist

Subject: ITP: r-cran-leidenbase -- GNU R and C/C++ Wrappers to Run the Leiden find_partition() Function
Package: wnpp
Owner: Andreas Tille <tille at debian.org>
Severity: wishlist

* Package name    : r-cran-leidenbase
  Version         : 0.1.11
  Upstream Author : Brent Ewing,
* URL             : https://cran.r-project.org/package=leidenbase
* License         : GPL-3
  Programming Lang: GNU R
  Description     : GNU R and C/C++ Wrappers to Run the Leiden find_partition() Function
 An R to C/C++ interface that runs the Leiden community
 detection algorithm to find a basic partition (). It runs the
 equivalent of the 'leidenalg' find_partition() function, which is
 given in the 'leidenalg' distribution file
 'leiden/src/functions.py'. This package includes the
 required source code files from the official 'leidenalg'
 distribution and functions from the R 'igraph' package.

Remark: This package is maintained by Debian R Packages Maintainers at
   https://salsa.debian.org/r-pkg-team/r-cran-leidenbase


